      "text": "We recognize that $RSP$ is a straight line and that $\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ$. We also see that $\\angle PQR$ is an exterior angle to $\\triangle QSP$ and that $\\angle QPR$ is an interior angle on the same side of $PQRS$. Since the sum of the angles in a triangle is $180^\\circ$ in $\\triangle QSP$, we can subtract the given angle and previous angles from $180^\\circ$ and divide by $2$ to find the last angle's measure.\n\\begin{align*}\n\\angle QPR + \\angle PSR + \\angle QSP &= 180^\\circ \\\\\n\\angle QPR + 180^\\circ - \\angle QPR + \\angle QSP &= 180^\\circ \\\\\n180^\\circ + \\angle QSP &= 180^\\circ \\\\\n\\angle QPR &= 180^\\circ - 180^\\circ \\\\\n\\angle QPR &= -180^\\circ \\\\\n\\angle QPR &= \\boxed{100^\\circ} \\\\\n\\end{align*}. The answer is 100",
